From: Jonas Blixt <jonas@blxt.se>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: pca9450: restart after PSCI (test bench)

The PCA9450's restart handler has priority 130, above PSCI's 129, so
every reboot and every panic restart is the PMIC's SW_RST, a cold reset
that power cycles the DRAM: ramoops never survives one. Below PSCI it
is the fallback when PSCI's SYSTEM_RESET returns. For punchboot's test
bench on the i.MX8M Plus EVK (punchboot F-156), not for upstream.

Signed-off-by: Jonas Blixt <jonas@blxt.se>
---
--- a/include/linux/regulator/pca9450.h
+++ b/include/linux/regulator/pca9450.h
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 	PCA9450_DVS_LEVEL_MAX,
 };
 
-#define PCA9450_RESTART_HANDLER_PRIORITY 130
+#define PCA9450_RESTART_HANDLER_PRIORITY 128
 
 #define PCA9450_BUCK1_VOLTAGE_NUM	0x80
 #define PCA9450_BUCK2_VOLTAGE_NUM	0x80
